# Rank 1572 / CVE-2026-44167: phpseclib's ASN.1 decoder accepted
# object identifiers up to 4096 bytes, so a certificate carrying
# near-4KB OIDs drove outsized parsing work in every chain-verification
# consumer (resource exhaustion through an over-generous cap,
# CWE-400/CWE-770). _decodeOID in phpseclib/File/ASN1.php did `$len
# = strlen($content); if ($len > 4096) { return false; }` -- the cap
# existed but sat far above the largest real-world OIDs, and the
# decoder's per-byte arithmetic multiplies the cost. Pool commit
# d53d2021bc is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "ASN1: reduce length of
# supported OIDs from 4096 bytes to 128 bytes", citing OpenJDK's
# ObjectIdentifier limit): the threshold becomes `if ($len > 128)` --
# the constant alone changes, matching JDK behaviour. No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, threshold adequacy. The guard exists and runs on both
# sides -- the defect is only that its constant is larger than any
# legitimate input needs, the budget family of ranks 1534 and 1559
# from the other side: no rule can ask "is this parser's size cap
# within the protocol's realistic range" -- threshold adequacy is a
# domain judgement (the fix cites OpenJDK's 128-byte limit as the
# reference point). A binding on phpseclib's own OID decoder would
# detect this library rather than the weakness. Measured on the real
# code: scanning ASN1.php reports one finding at both revisions
# (unchanged; unrelated heuristic). No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1572 records the 4096-byte
# cap and the 128-byte form, both asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029:
# when threshold-adequacy vocabulary lands, the over-generous form
# must flip to expect.

test "rank1572: the oid cap sits at four kilobytes"
  lang php
  file phpseclib/File/ASN1.php
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  <?php

  class File_ASN1
  {
      function _decodeOID($content)
      {
          $pos = 0;
          $len = strlen($content);

          if ($len > 4096) {
              //user_error('Object Identifier size is limited to 4096 bytes');
              return false;
          }

          $oid = '';
          while ($pos < $len) {
              $byte = ord($content[$pos++]);
              $oid .= dechex($byte >> 7);
              if (~$byte & 0x80) {
                  $oid .= '.';
              }
          }
          return $oid;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1572: the fix tightens the cap to the jdk limit"
  lang php
  file phpseclib/File/ASN1.php
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  <?php

  class File_ASN1
  {
      function _decodeOID($content)
      {
          $pos = 0;
          $len = strlen($content);

          if ($len > 128) {
              //user_error('Object Identifier size is limited to 128 bytes');
              return false;
          }

          $oid = '';
          while ($pos < $len) {
              $byte = ord($content[$pos++]);
              $oid .= dechex($byte >> 7);
              if (~$byte & 0x80) {
                  $oid .= '.';
              }
          }
          return $oid;
      }
  }
  ```
